mulator; every failure returns undefined so the registration is refused with the pre-existing fail-closed CREATOR_CLOSE_UNAVAILABLE before any staging. Upstream binding is real: prepareExistingCreatorGeneration authenticates the anchor signature and pins projection kind v3-live-generation-2, and buildPreparedV3LiveMint requires the durable head candidate bytes to equal the projection. Defensive copying is genuine on both ends: validateSnapshot (ct-merkle.ts:321-341) copies every peak, snapshot() copies out, and captureSnapshot in the unchanged verifier copies again, so no mutable alias reaches registered or authenticated continuity. Result shape is unchanged except epoch/successorEpoch widening to number (proved exactly by the Equal<> type contract, including exact key roster, epoch-0 compatibility, 1->2, and later epoch 3); the overflow guard rejects non-safe/negative/MAX_SAFE_INTEGER epochs at bind before staging, and successor identity (currentEpoch === epoch+1, same objectId, same genesisAnchorDigest) is enforced before stageCombinedGeneration/terminalize/adoption-fact install. Retained gates reconcile exactly with the reporter JSON I parsed: focused 1/1 (corrected and evidence captures), retained 128/128 across 16 files after the disclosed 127/128 stale expectedRoomHead key-roster expectation, browser 9/6/24/27. D.110a, campaigns, and the separately authorized Fable 0b0b research are all recorded as zero/out-of-gate. The blocking defect is not in the production code but in the GREEN's proof obligations: the accepted plan (plan-v2.md:93734-93745) and the confirmation disposition (:93824, 'the hostile-carrier reason is mandatory rather than optional') made the hostile-carrier refusal matrix and the skipped-epoch/substituted-successor/overflow refusals mandatory GREEN proofs, and the delivered fixture contains none of them, with no disclosure of the omission in the GREEN ledger or plan record. The entire security surface added by this slice therefore has zero adve